<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neriglissar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 560–556 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neriglissar was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> from 560 to 556 BCE. A leading official and son-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a>, he took the throne after the murder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amel-marduk">Amel-Marduk</a>, which he probably organised. In 557 BCE he campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appuashu">Appuashu</a> of Pirindu. His young son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/labashi-marduk">Labashi-Marduk</a> succeeded him but was overthrown within months by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabonidus">Nabonidus</a>.</p></div>
